## Slot vocabulary ({{slot-count}} slots inherited or declared)

Event memorials inherit `:mm/Memory` plus type-specific required slots:

- **`lifecycle-position`** (required) — when in the lifecycle this event fires
- **`default-severity`** — `audit` / `warn` / `block` — what severity rules inherit when triggered by this event
- **`applicable-actor-classes`** — which actor types can trigger this event
- **`triggered-by-hook`** — hook script path or sentinel keyword
- **`substrate-correctness-criticality`** — `tier-0` / `tier-1` / `tier-2` / `tier-3`

{{slot-table}}

## Severity gradient

Default-severity governs what severity rules inherit when triggered by this event:

- **`audit`** — observe but don't act
- **`warn`** — surface as soft block
- **`block`** — refuse + interrupt

Individual rules can OVERRIDE the default per their own `enforcement:` declaration.

## Applicable actor classes

Some events apply only to specific actor types:

- All actors (`:any`)
- AI actors
- Human actors
- System actors

The field declares which actor types CAN trigger this event.

## Criticality tiers

- **`tier-0`** — substrate-correctness depends on firing (e.g., `session-start` surfaces active disciplines; `pre-tool-use` bypasses substrate-correctness rules if not fired)
- **`tier-1`** — high-frequency but not substrate-correctness (e.g., `post-commit` validation can be deferred)
- **`tier-2` / `tier-3`** — lower-priority observation events

## Canonical body structure

```markdown
## What this event signals

<When the event fires, what conditions warrant it.>

## Data payload

<What context information accompanies the event (tool name, file
path, prompt text, etc.).>

## Hook integration

<Which hook scripts in etc/hooks/ trigger this event; the
substrate machinery binding.>

## Rules that fire on this event

<Catalog of rule memorials that consume this event via
triggered-by: edges.  Or note "none yet" if pre-population.>

## See also

<Adjacent events, related rules, governing decisions.>
```

## What an event memorial is NOT

- **Not a hook script** — the hook layer FIRES the event; the event memorial is the CONTENT
- **Not a rule** — events trigger rules; events themselves don't fire actions
- **Not a notification** — events are SUBSTRATE-LEVEL lifecycle markers; notifications are UI-layer constructs

